Wizards *always* get the Magicbane as their first gift, unless it already
exists in a bones pile that you've overlooked on a level where you've
been. If you sacrifice long enough, you're bound to get it.

If your god gives you a long sword, however (as your second gift, for
instance), it's good to train up the skill to Basic which you otherwise
couldn't; in the later game you might want to wield something more beefy.

That said, I currently have a wizard on the up stairs to the Planes
wielding the +3 Magicbane, who never wielded anything else except her
starting quarterstaff and the silver dagger she found in a shop on DL 3.

